 Formerly the Review artifact. The single living document **Refine** maintains for a **Task set**: what the latest pass fixed, the smells it left, and the SHA of the tree it describes. Each pass supersedes rather than appends — the **Refiner** reads the previous report and writes the current one, carrying forward what is still true; prior documents stay under the set's directory and every reader takes the latest by timestamp. A **Task artifact**, so it never enters an **Implementation commit**; reaching a PR is an explicit human act. Humans meet it as a pointer at the **HITL gate prompt** and in the **Task set detail view**, and an **Assist session**'s prompt names its path.
 _Avoid_: Review artifact, review report, findings file, smell list
 
+**Exploration report**:
+The code as one Explorer found it before anyone built in a **Task set**: where things live, which seam owns what, the invariants around them, and the SHA of the tree it describes. A flat `exploration.md` beside the spec and the **Progress record**, listed between them — what was decided, what exists, what happened. Written once, when absent; nothing computes its freshness. A builder edits it only to correct a line its own attempt falsified (ADR-0262). A **Task artifact**, never committed.
+_Avoid_: exploration notes, code map, journal
+
+**Explore directive**:
+The set-level manifest key `"explore": true` with which a set's author asks for an **Exploration report**. Opt-in, where `verify` and `refine` are opt-out: absent or `false` means the set never explores. Set when two or more AFK tasks touch the same seam and a later one depends on how an earlier one shapes it. Outside the agent-directive objects `"verifier"` and `"refiner"`; its twin `"explorer"` steers the pass's agents and effort but never opts a set in (ADR-0262).
+_Avoid_: explore flag, exploration threshold
+
+**Explorer**:
+The agent that writes the **Exploration report**: a fresh agent handed the set's manifest listing, its task bodies and its spec, that records the code as found in the area those tasks touch — every claim naming a path or a symbol, about one page, stating the tree it describes — and nothing about prior art, which stays in the builder's own frame (ADR-0262). Spawned under the **Read-only agent posture**; its runs are **Captured runs** of phase `explore`. `pop tasks explore` runs it by hand on any set, whatever its **Explore directive** says, and replaces the report; a pass that does not finish writes nothing.
+_Avoid_: mapper, scout, surveyor
+
+**Explore phase**:
+The **Drain**'s step that runs the **Explorer** once, at the head of the drain, before the first task is selected — for a set whose **Explore directive** asks for it and that has no **Exploration report** yet. Absent means write it; present means reuse it, and the drain spends nothing on exploring. `[work.explore]` gates it for the whole machine and, alone among agent phases, defaults on: the set's own directive is the trigger, so a set that never asked costs nothing. It declines for a **Human completion**, as the refine step does. It is the one agent phase that stops a drain: a pass that gives up after the standard per-phase retry cap parks it at EXPLORE-FAILED (**Explore park**), and no drain explores a parked set again. Agents and effort resolve CLI flags → the set's `"explorer"` object → `[work.explore]` → `[work.implement].agents` (ADR-0262).
+_Avoid_: explore step, pre-flight
+
+**Explore park**:
+The EXPLORE-FAILED status: a READY **Task set** whose **Explore directive** asks for exploration, that has no **Exploration report**, and whose latest **Captured run** of phase `explore` was not the human's interrupt. It is derived, never stored — `ResolveExplorePark` reads the run and the report and the refresh lays it over READY, so nothing re-selects the set and no daemon re-explores it in a loop. A pass that gives up before any agent runs — every preset unavailable — files one `explore` run with its reason, so the park holds for it too. It is not BLOCKED: that status means a human owes a decision about the work. Parking appends one set-level **Progress record** naming the phase and the reason. Three doors leave it: `pop tasks explore <set>` writes the report, `pop tasks implement <set> --skip-explore` drains the set once unexplored, and `"explore": false` retracts the declaration (ADR-0262).
+_Avoid_: explore blocked, explore-parked
+
+**Explore mark**:
+Whether a **Task set** whose **Explore directive** asks for exploration got its **Exploration report** — `explored` or `unexplored` — carried beside its status as the **Verification mark** is, with the reason an unexplored set has none (not yet run, or the pass failed) as detail beside it rather than a value inside it. A set that never asked carries no mark. `ResolveExploreMark` is the one read-side resolution: the refresh lays it over every row, and the **Explore park** is derived from it. The Work row, its detail view, `pop work status` and `pop tasks status` render it, and the detail view and the sign-off gate carry the report as a pointer — its path and the tree its header records, never its body (ADR-0262).
+_Avoid_: explored status, explore badge
